Title: Build V8's ia32 stack-scanning assembly on Windows
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

  lld-link : error : undefined symbol: _PushAllRegistersAndIterateStack
  >>> referenced by deps/v8/src/heap/base/stack.cc:202
  >>>               v8_base_without_compiler.lib(stack.obj)

PushAllRegistersAndIterateStack pushes the callee-saved registers so cppgc's
conservative stack scan can see them, and it is hand-written assembly chosen
per architecture. The OS=="win" branch of v8.gyp lists only x64 and arm64;
there is no ia32 case, so on a 32-bit Windows build nothing supplies the
symbol. The OS!="win" branch has had an ia32 case all along.

The fix is to name the file that already exists. V8 ships no ia32 masm
counterpart, and does not need one: ia32/push_registers_asm.cc carries a
_WIN32 branch that switches to .att_syntax and declares the symbol as
_PushAllRegistersAndIterateStack, with the leading underscore a cdecl symbol
takes on Win32. That branch is intact; it was simply never reached from here.

x64 is the exception rather than ia32. The comment above this block records
why: a change to push_registers_asm.cc in V8 v12.8 meant x64 had to move to
push_registers_masm.asm on Windows even under ClangCL. Nothing in that change
affected the ia32 file.

Module-level asm() is a GNU extension, so this needs Clang. That is not a new
constraint: vcbuild.bat refuses to build Node 24 or later on Windows without
ClangCL.

diff --git a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
@@ -2056,6 +2056,18 @@
                   '<(V8_ROOT)/src/heap/base/asm/x64/push_registers_masm.asm',
                 ],
               }],
+              # ia32 keeps the .cc, which x64 no longer can. The file is written
+              # for this: its _WIN32 branch emits .att_syntax and declares
+              # _PushAllRegistersAndIterateStack with the leading underscore a
+              # cdecl symbol takes on Win32. There is no ia32 masm counterpart to
+              # switch to, and none is needed. Module-level asm() is a GNU
+              # extension, which is fine here because Node 24 and later require
+              # ClangCL on Windows regardless.
+              ['_toolset == "host" and host_arch == "ia32" or _toolset == "target" and target_arch=="ia32"', {
+                'sources': [
+                  '<(V8_ROOT)/src/heap/base/asm/ia32/push_registers_asm.cc',
+                ],
+              }],
               ['_toolset == "host" and host_arch == "arm64" or _toolset == "target" and target_arch=="arm64"', {
                 'conditions': [
                   ['clang==1', {
